rrected to 19 doors, carting count = 49 EA, not 45.\",\n          \"recommendation\": \"Update carting rollup to use Item 12's count of 19 doors. Revised minimum: 49 EA.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"severity\": \"WARNING\",\n          \"check\": \"CROSS-REFERENCE\",\n          \"description\": \"The carting count was produced by Group BC executor who did NOT have access to final Group A quantities. The rollup should be recalculated using final Group A numbers.\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Executor notes: 'This count depends on final quantities from GROUP A items (8, 12-22) which were not measured in this batch.'\",\n          \"recommendation\": \"Recalculate carting using final quantities: 19 doors + 1 fridge (or 2) + 4 access panels + 2 glazing + dental equipment + misc. Should be ~49-55 EA.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"severity\": \"INFO\",\n          \"check\": \"UNIT CONSISTENCY\",\n          \"description\": \"Unit EA interpretation still ambiguous — per fixture vs per cart load. Executor assumed per fixture which is more conservative.\",\n          \"evidence\": \"Task packet flagged this ambiguity. Executor assumed per-fixture count.\",\n          \"recommendation\": \"Clarify with bid coordinator. Per-fixture count of ~49 is reasonable.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"revised_quantity\": 49,\n      \"escalate_to_doug\": true,\n      \"confidence_assessment\": \"LOW — internal inconsistency found, depends on all other items, unit ambiguous\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"escalation_summary\": \"PRIORITY ESCALATION TO DOUG:\\n\\n1. **Item 11 (4th Floor Ceiling R&R) — HIGHEST PRIORITY**: 3,500 SF is a blind guess with no 4th floor drawings. Recommend pricing 50% and 100% scenarios. Also flag 4th floor ceiling TYPE (ACT vs GWB) — cost differs 5x. This is the single highest-risk demo item.\\n\\n2. **Item 23 (Carting) — MATH ERROR**: Internal rollup uses 15 doors but Item 12 says 19. Minimum correction to 49 EA. Also clarify EA = per fixture vs per load.\\